1blz|a|Of or relating to mycology, or the fungi.	j:1vu0,111,5~1vu0,111,5
1bq8|n|A story of great but unknown age which originally embodied a belief regarding some fact or phenomenon of experience, and in which often the forces of nature and of the soul are personified; an ancient legend of a god, a hero, the origin of a race, etc.; a wonder story of prehistoric origin; a popular fable which is, or has been, received as historical. ; A person or thing existing only in imagination, or whose actual existence is not verifiable.	a:26ao,130,12;1kcb,75,4~26ao,130,12;1kcb,75,4
1bqm|n|The science which treats of myths; a treatise on myths. ; A body of myths; esp., the collective myths which describe the gods of a heathen people; as, the mythology of the Greeks.	n:xxk,147,4~xxk,147,4
